energy_arc:
Alaap: patient, brooding exposition in the mandra saptak establishing ancient gravity;
Mukhada: colossal doom groove drops, locking sitar and crushing rhythm into sam Sa;
Manjha: tempo stays steady while the melody recedes into dark lower depths;
Mukhada Return: the heavy theme slams back with reinforced authority;
Antara: dynamic lift into madhya and taar saptak, ramping emotional tension;
Taan: virtuosic chaugun cascades driving the rhythmic tension to its peak;
Mukhada Climax: the definitive, heaviest statement of the gat under full distortion;
Outro: heavy feedback and tanpura ringing out as the final Sa decays into silence.
